                sum[lb * D + k] += pts[i * D + k];
            }
        }
        ```
        *Critique*: Too many atomic operations ($n \times (1+D)$). With $n=2,000,000$, that's $18 \times 10^6$ atomic operations per iteration. This will likely be slow.

    *   **Approach B (Thread-local buffers/Array Reduction)**:
        ```c
        double sum[K * D];
        long cnt[K];
        // ...
        #pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum[:K*D], cnt[:K])
        for (long i = 0; i < n; i++) {
